@@ -0,0 +1,146 @@
+# Visual Lab
+
+A frontend-only extension to the existing Amin Mansori portfolio. The new
+collection lives at `/lab` (German) and `/en/lab` (English).
+
+## Apply the patch
+
+The patch was prepared against `aminmansuri1377/portfolio-pwa`, branch `main`,
+commit `996c0650ed36da50f7e03d78f2ba6a58685136c6` (`mobile new ui`).
+It is a standard Git diff, not a replacement project or a dependency upgrade.
+
+From the repository root, with your current work saved:
+
+```sh
+git switch -c feature/visual-lab
+git apply --check portfolio-visual-lab.patch
+git apply portfolio-visual-lab.patch
+npm ci
+npm run dev
+```
+
+Open `http://localhost:3000/lab` or `http://localhost:3000/en/lab`.
+For a production build:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+npm start
+```
+
+No new packages, API endpoints, database, environment variables, model downloads,
+image downloads or hosting configuration are needed. The existing `next/font`
+configuration still needs its usual font access during a first clean build.
+
+If `git apply --check` reports a conflict, stop and compare your current changes
+to the base above. Do not force the patch or discard unrelated work.
+
+To reverse the patch before making further changes to its files:
+
+```sh
+git apply --reverse --check portfolio-visual-lab.patch
+git apply --reverse portfolio-visual-lab.patch
+```
+
+## Integration surface
+
+Only two pre-existing files are changed:
+
+- `pages/index.js`: imports and renders a lightweight Visual Lab invitation
+  between Projects and Contact.
+- `components/layout/Navbar.jsx`: adds the Visual Lab link on desktop and mobile.
+
+The rest of the implementation is additive. Existing project cards, case studies,
+hero, translations, global styles, footer, PWA behavior and dependency files are
+not edited. The home-page invitation has no WebGL canvas or running animation
+loop; the new navigation link opts out of route prefetching.
+
+## The collection
+
+| Demo | Experience | Interaction |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| AURA | Procedural Three.js headphones | Finishes, orbit, exploded view, wireframe, keyboard camera angle |
+| FOLIO | Editorial portfolio fragment | Three original vector-art compositions and animated scene changes |
+| PULSE | Analytics interface | Local date ranges, chart inspection, order search and status filter |
+| FLUX | Generative sculpture | GLSL surface deformation, sphere/knot, palette, wireframe |
+| KINETIC | Spring-motion studio | Pointer dragging, keyboard controls, spring presets, stiffness and damping |
+| ATELIER | Product storefront | CSS-rendered products, finish variants, sample bag, coupon and totals |
+| ORBIT | Particle galaxy | 6,000 particles, three/five arms, spiral tension, palette and orbit |
+| PALETTE | Typographic art-direction tool | Editable words, theme, scale, tracking, weight, layouts and CSS copy |
+| RELAY | Kanban workspace | Sample tasks, drag and drop, status menus, priority filter and reset |
+
+These are original concept studies, not claims about real client projects.
+Products, analytics and tasks are clearly identified as examples. All state is
+held in React memory and resets when a demo is closed or unmounted. No request
+submits a purchase, message or task to a server. No localStorage, cookies or
+analytics are introduced.
+
+The copy button in an experiment creates a direct URL such as
+`/en/lab?demo=aura`. The `demo` value is checked against the local catalog.
+The page uses the original site's locale switch and SEO component.
+
+## Structure
+
+```text
+pages/lab.jsx
+lib/lab.js                            Catalog and DE/EN gallery copy
+components/sections/VisualLabSection.jsx
+components/lab/VisualLab.jsx          Gallery and route state
+components/lab/LabArtwork.jsx         Lightweight gallery-cover artwork
+components/lab/LabDialog.jsx          Accessible native dialog and lazy loaders
+components/lab/spatial/               Three.js scenes and controls
+components/lab/frontend/              Editorial, spring and typography studies
+components/lab/interfaces/            Dashboard, storefront and Kanban studies
+styles/visual-lab*.module.css          Gallery and home invitation
+styles/lab-*.module.css               Isolated experiment styles
+```
+
+To add an experiment, extend the catalog and both locale dictionaries in
+`lib/lab.js`, add its cover to `LabArtwork.jsx`, and add its component to the
+matching demo dispatcher. Update the collection count and introductory copy.
+
+## Performance and accessibility
+
+- Gallery covers use local CSS and SVG instead of nine simultaneous canvases.
+- The demo groups are dynamically imported when needed.
+- Only the open spatial demo renders continuously; the hero pauses while the
+  dialog is open. Offscreen/hidden-tab rendering is paused, and DPR is capped.
+- Three.js geometry, particles and studio lighting are procedural and local.
+- Scene resources and listeners are cleaned up when components unmount.
+- Reduced-motion preferences and the gallery's motion toggle are respected.
+- A native modal dialog provides focus trapping, Escape handling and an inert
+  background. Focus returns to the opener. Lenis is paused without blocking
+  native scrolling inside the dialog.
+- Drag interactions have button, keyboard or status-menu alternatives.
+- Loading/import failures expose a retry action. Clipboard failure exposes
+  selectable text instead of silently claiming success.
+- WebGL2 availability is checked before creating a renderer. On unsupported
+  browsers or context loss, an illustrated fallback remains usable. GPU-only
+  controls are disabled honestly; supported preview controls remain available.
+
+## Verification
+
+The implementation was production-built with the repository's existing lockfile
+and inspected in the browser. Desktop checks covered category filters, both
+locales, all nine dialogs, representative interactions, Escape and focus return.
+Responsive layout checks used narrow iframe viewports as well as the desktop
+viewport. The patch was also checked against a clean checkout of its stated base.
+
+The QA browser has WebGL disabled. The fallback paths were visually inspected;
+actual GPU shader compilation and the GPU-rendered appearance could not be
+observed in that environment. The scene code, shader compatibility, framing and
+resource lifecycle were separately reviewed. Check the three GPU scenes on a
+WebGL2-capable browser before publishing.
+
+## Design references
+
+The work takes general interaction and composition inspiration from these
+first-party references. Their source code, branding, models and image assets are
+not copied into this project.
+
+- Bruno Simon: https://bruno-simon.com/
+- Lusion, Gemini: https://v2.lusion.co/work/gemini/
+- Linear, interface design: https://linear.app/now/behind-the-latest-design-refresh
+- Three.js, on-demand rendering: https://threejs.org/manual/pages/rendering-on-demand.html
+
+The new route is intended for the portfolio's existing deployment process. This
+patch does not publish a site or change the live GitHub repository.
